==============================================================================
Third-party software and services
==============================================================================

This repository contains **no third-party source code**. It configures and
drives the following components, each under its own license:

- OpenSSH (https://www.openssh.com/)
  The SSH client and server this repository enables and uses. The Windows
  build shipped as the `OpenSSH.Server` / `OpenSSH.Client` optional features
  is distributed by Microsoft.
  Licensed under a BSD-style license (OpenBSD).
  Why used: it is the transport for every remote operation in this repo.

- OpenSSH for Windows (https://github.com/PowerShell/Win32-OpenSSH)
  The standalone MSI port used only as a fallback when the optional feature
  is unavailable. This repository does not redistribute it.
  Licensed under the MIT License (Microsoft's port) over the upstream
  BSD-style OpenSSH code.
  Why used: older or trimmed Windows images may lack the optional feature.

- PowerShell (https://github.com/PowerShell/PowerShell)
  The default shell on the remote side. Windows PowerShell 5.1 ships with
  Windows; PowerShell 7 is optional.
  Licensed under the MIT License (PowerShell 7).
  Why used: `host/` scripts are PowerShell.

- Python (https://www.python.org/)
  Runtime for `tools/` (documentation and secret checks). Standard library
  only, except `tools/make_social_preview.py` which uses numpy and Pillow.
  Licensed under the Python Software Foundation License.
  Why used: the repository's self-checks run in CI on Linux.

- Windows (https://www.microsoft.com/windows)
  The target operating system. No Microsoft code is redistributed here.

==============================================================================
Credentials
==============================================================================

This repository stores **no credentials**. SSH private keys stay in the
operator's `~/.ssh/`; host names, user names and ports live in
`host/host.conf`, which is not tracked by git.

See docs/SECRETS.md for the location index.
